WEBVTT

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.400
"Kodomo no Odocha"

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.740
That rumor that I love you

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.370
is true, yes it is.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:20.870
You can't ignore it either.

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.460
Whether you're awake or asleep,

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.090
please don't be embarrassed.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.640
Is it a sin if I sneak into your heart

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:40.350
by ridding you...

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:43.520
...of your other love?

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.110
At sunset,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:50.610
when the children go home,

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.570
Today's incident is burning love!

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:58.450
You can tell it accurately.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.540
7 O'Clock News!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:04.330
Please, our relationship...

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.960
Please don't blame it on the true kiss

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.800
In a city without light,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:15.680
let's burn the fire of love.

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:19.100
Don't be so easy going

00:01:19.180 --> 00:01:21.390
The existence is a mistake

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:24.890
You're asking for something not there.

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.240
I'm Kurata Sana, a 6th grader
and TV personality.

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:41.620
Sagami Rei-kun, my chauffeur
and manager, and former boyfriend.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:45.040
My Aoki Laureate prize-winning Mama.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:49.290
Hayama Akito, my natural
enemy and good friend.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:52.420
Where's your dad?

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.380
You want to know about my dad?

00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:03.060
Oh, I don't have a dad!

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:05.430
Really, that's all there is to it.

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:08.100
Then, your mom has been
single the whole time?

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:12.110
Uh-uh. She got married when she
was 18, and was divorced at 20.

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:14.070
So, that was your dad?

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:16.440
Uh-uh. Nope.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.110
Well, what, then?

00:02:18.110 --> 00:02:20.280
Sorry. I know it's not fair to you,

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:23.790
what with me knowing all
about the Hayama family,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.450
but I think you're going
to find out soon enough.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:37.130
Whew, whenever I put on a serious face,
my shoulders get stiff.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.300
Oh yeah, you haven't forgotten
that we're having outdoor school

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.800
starting tomorrow, right?

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:45.770
You haven't forgotten that we're
having outdoor school, right!?

00:02:48.140 --> 00:02:51.020
Oh, no! I forgot to buy snacks.

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.820
She's not being very
straight with me, huh?

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:05.160
"The Summer of My Promise - Part I"

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.750
I thought you were only supposed
to bring ¥500 worth of snacks.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:12.750
That's why I'm taking a little from each
of them, so that it adds up to ¥500 total.

00:03:14.090 --> 00:03:18.090
You didn't have to buy
¥500,000's worth, though.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.590
So, about work, once you
get back from outdoor school,

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.090
it will be summer vacation,
and there's this tasty TV drama that--

00:03:22.090 --> 00:03:24.430
Absolutely no way!

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:25.760
Why not?

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:28.100
I really like the stage.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.980
Live! Live!

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.020
I like doing live performances,
where you're not allowed outtakes!

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:36.020
That's a shame.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:37.020
She's calling...

00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:39.030
Mama is calling me!

00:03:39.030 --> 00:03:40.450
Bye!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:48.700
Mama, did you call?

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.710
I called my brains out,
with this conch shell.

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:55.040
Sit down there.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.090
Not there!

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:03.720
Sana, how about we fulfill your promise?

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:07.050
It looks like this...
is going to get very serious.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.770
I'd like to start writing
that essay about you and me

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.730
that we made that promise over.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:15.940
The two conditions that were
necessary for that to happen

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:18.070
have been more than met.

00:04:18.070 --> 00:04:22.070
One of them was that I would
become a famous novelist.

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:24.740
The other one was that you would
become a little more famous

00:04:24.740 --> 00:04:27.410
than other children in general.

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:32.410
Mm-hmm. I see... I had a hunch
this would be coming up soon.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.960
So, when will you have
the manuscript finished?

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.040
You're going to write the
whole book at once, right?

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.380
I just have to put together everything
I've already written up to now,

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:44.720
so, I'd say about three days.

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:46.720
Three days?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.050
When will it be published?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:50.970
Around the time summer vacation
is over, probably.

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:54.060
I see...

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.190
Mm-hmm, all right. I won't be
able to help you out at all,

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:58.610
but good luck with it, Mama!

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.400
Enjoy your outdoor school!

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.940
Right!

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:10.740
Sana, why does a girl like you...

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:13.080
Why are you wearing
the bathroom slippers!?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.410
--Outdoor! Outdoor! Ya-hoo-hoo!
--Don't go running around the house

00:05:15.410 --> 00:05:18.750
--For love and courage, it's
outdoor school! Here we go, out-door-door!
--wearing those things! Stop!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.090
--Sana-chan is going, woo-hoo-hoo!
--Hold it! Hold it! Hold it! Hold it!

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:23.420
Out-out door-door, outdoor!

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.300
"Outdoor school!
Everyone gather around!!"

00:05:23.420 --> 00:05:25.380
We're going! We're going, right?

00:05:25.380 --> 00:05:26.430
We're going!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.430
Enough rest-- okay!

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.100
Appetite-- okay!

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:31.680
Uh-oh... I'm not so sure
about being all backed up.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.680
What are you talking about? You get
through constipation by force of nerve!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.020
You dish out full power
to your lower body, right?

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:41.020
I get it. You work out your
constipation with "guts"!

00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:43.690
G- good morning, Sugita-san.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:46.360
Oh, no, Sana-chan...

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.030
Good morning, Tsuyoshi-kun.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:52.700
Now see here, line up there!
Get on the bus at once! At once!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:53.370
Did you bring your hair dryer?

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:55.040
--Nope. I did bring
my curling iron, though.
--Well...

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:55.870
Let me borrow it, okay?

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.710
The girls in 3rd Class
are a bit ostentatious,

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.080
don't you think, Mitsuya-sensei?

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.710
Indeed! What are we to do with them?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.670
It's your makeup that's ostentatious,
you wrinkled hag.

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:15.390
Who was that!? Who was it
that said that just now!?

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.390
"Wrinkled hag," he said!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.390
Wrinkled hag!

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.730
Now, now, Ando-sensei, it's too early
in the morning to be getting worked up.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.740
Principal! It's because you're too laid
back that our school isn't any good!

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:30.780
Have you heard about the
poor quality of 3rd Class!?

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.540
Principal, it's because
you're so laid back that--

00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:38.000
They'll turn out fine-fine.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.370
Oh, there he is!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.370
It's Narunaru!

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:43.670
Principal Narunaru is finally
making his first appearance!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.340
--Narunaru!

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:47.010
Thank you, thank you!

00:06:47.010 --> 00:06:49.840
I'm uneasy about where this is going...

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:55.810
We're off!

00:06:57.390 --> 00:07:00.690
So, where are we going?

00:07:00.690 --> 00:07:03.150
Driver, do you know?

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:05.360
This isn't any good...

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.740
Hey, drive, would you?

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:09.740
The first day will be
in the Aishu highlands.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:12.410
The second day will be
climbing up Mt. Daichitake.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:16.080
You're one astounding idiot, huh?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.410
So there you are, Hayama!

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:20.330
I'm the one who's astounded!

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:22.630
Imagine, you, not skipping
a school activity!

00:07:24.090 --> 00:07:26.960
So, how many days is this trip?

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:30.050
Three days and two nights.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.340
You guys are both numbskulls.

00:07:32.340 --> 00:07:34.010
What kind of snacks did you bring?

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:35.680
I brought sashimi.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.010
You call that a snack?

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:39.390
I wonder if mayonnaise is a snack.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.690
Outdoor school is three days
and two nights...

00:07:47.690 --> 00:07:50.360
Once I get home, Mama will
have finished her manuscript,

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:54.370
and by the end of summer vacation,
it will be published everywhere...

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:56.370
The commotion that will follow
is a foregone conclusion.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:01.370
The media will make a story out of
Mama and me. But that's not the problem.

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:04.670
Our mother-daughter
relationship will be...

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:11.720
What a dumb look on your face.

00:08:11.720 --> 00:08:14.050
What are you pulling!?

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:16.390
I- I was just sleeping with
my eyes open for a little bit!

00:08:16.390 --> 00:08:18.720
What are you, a goldfish?

00:08:18.720 --> 00:08:21.390
So, did you want something?

00:08:21.390 --> 00:08:23.390
My dad came home from
the hospital yesterday.

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:25.060
Oh, really!?

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.060
He said to tell you thanks.

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.230
That's terrific.
He doesn't need to thank me.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:32.990
The relationship between your
dad and I is too close for that.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.280
Sing for us, Sana-chan!

00:08:36.990 --> 00:08:41.330
Y- you mean here...?
It's kind of embarrassing, but...

00:08:41.330 --> 00:08:44.000
All right! I'll give it a shot!

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.330
♪ Outdoors, outdoors, hello to you! ♪

00:08:46.330 --> 00:08:48.340
♪ Heading to the mountains,
hello to you! ♪

00:08:48.340 --> 00:08:50.340
♪ The bus is going-going,
you're going-going too! ♪

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.340
♪ Gently, violently, the bus is going! ♪

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.680
♪ With the love and hopes
of everyone on board. ♪

00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:56.340
♪ Everyone has ¥500 worth of snacks. ♪

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:58.350
♪ Fly, fly, outdoors! Fight, outdoors! ♪

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.680
♪ Thoroughly refreshing outdoor school! ♪

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:03.020
♪ --Are you ready!? Are you ready!? ♪
--That's dangerous!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.690
♪ --Here we go, moving down the road! ♪
--You can't stand there!

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:06.690
♪ --Going clown this country road! ♪
--You're gonna die!

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.690
♪ Woah, this country road is treacherous! ♪

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.690
♪ But still, this country road is fun! ♪

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:11.690
Yo, Tanuki! How's it going?

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.360
This guy's got some impressive tackle!

00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:15.030
Firefly Inn, it's called! Firefly Inn!

00:09:15.030 --> 00:09:16.360
I wonder if there are
any real fireflies around.

00:09:16.360 --> 00:09:18.030
I've never seen one before.
Their tushies light up.

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:21.370
Everybody, please split up
into each of your rooms and wash up!

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:26.370
Supper is at 6 o'clock...
6 o'clock in the banquet hall...

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.380
Nobody is listening, right?

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:34.470
Listen to me, if you don't listen,
you won't be able to eat dinner.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:38.760
--"We humbly partake of this meal."
--Y- you did listen to me?

00:09:40.010 --> 00:09:41.680
Oh, meat! Meat!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.560
You can have the fatty part.

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:49.020
Sana-chan, the meat is going fast.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:51.020
Oh, meat! Meat!

00:09:51.020 --> 00:09:52.690
Ooh, the meat is all gone!

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:54.360
Sana-chan, you're too slow.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:59.490
Teppanyaki is a battle! Those who are
too slow are not fit to eat the meat!

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.700
I still have my fatty part.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.790
I'll take this meat!

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:07.370
Sana-chan, that's raw!

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:12.380
Raw is fine! I like anything that's raw!

00:10:12.380 --> 00:10:15.050
Where is it you're pointing?

00:10:15.050 --> 00:10:17.380
--Amazing! Kurata is eating the meat raw.
--Sana-chan is wild!

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:20.390
--She's not even putting any sauce on it.
--She's a wild child.

00:10:20.390 --> 00:10:23.600
It's like Kurata doesn't
have a care in the world.

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:31.230
You shouldn't be throwing your pill--

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:36.320
Say, let's all stay up until morning!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.990
--Absolutely!
--Okay! Okay!

00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:40.990
Mm-hmm! Let's stay up, no matter what!

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.660
That's what you all say...

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:45.660
...but all of you ended up
falling asleep.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:48.000
Ah, this is no fun.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.670
They're all still children, after all.

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.670
Guess I'll go to the bathroom.

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:57.510
I'll work up enough force of nerve
and guts to achieve regularity again!

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:08.140
Right about now, Mama's manuscript
must be coming right along...

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.360
Yo.

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.190
What are you doing, Hayama!?
Oh, you startled me!

00:11:16.190 --> 00:11:17.690
Sana-chan's been shocked senseless!

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:18.690
Bathroom, huh?

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.700
Yeah, constipation has me over a barrel.

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:23.370
But with enough force of nerve,
I'm going to be nice and regular!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:25.370
And is that usually the sort
of thing you make a girl say!?

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:28.700
No, you said all that on your own!

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.630
W- what are you staring at!?
Oh, you want to go at it!?

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:41.720
What are you looking away for?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:43.050
W- well...

00:11:43.050 --> 00:11:45.850
You've been acting strange lately,
you know?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:48.390
Spacing off all the time, and stuff.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.730
Is something the matter?

00:11:50.730 --> 00:11:52.730
"You're sharp, Hayama!"

00:11:52.730 --> 00:11:55.730
Mm-mm, nothing really.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:59.530
Is that right?

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:03.160
It's possible that maybe you...

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:09.700
Maybe you... what!?

00:12:16.090 --> 00:12:20.090
There's something that occurs
to me once in a while...

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.180
It's possible that maybe you...

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:27.760
The principal...?

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:29.640
That's Narunaru's laugh.

00:12:31.430 --> 00:12:34.350
What fun, what fun, what fun,
what fun, what fun!

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.360
What fun this turning out to be-be!

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:38.570
What fun!

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:43.700
What are you guys doing?

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.990
What, you ask...?

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.410
"Midnight Teachers' Banquet!"

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:48.410
The secret's out!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:50.740
This is sneaky, you teachers!

00:12:50.740 --> 00:12:51.410
Sushi?

00:12:51.410 --> 00:12:54.370
Kurata! Hayama! What time
do you think it is!?

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.040
Y- yeah! It's 2 o'clock already!

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:57.380
Kurata-san, this is bad
for your complexion!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.050
That goes the same for you,
Mitsuya-sensei, right?

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.420
Sushi...

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:03.720
S- such children!

00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.090
It's because you are poor educators

00:13:05.090 --> 00:13:06.090
--that these students let
things go to their heads!
--Sushi...

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:07.590
--that these students let
things go to their heads!
--Hayama, you like sushi?

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:08.800
--that these students let
things go to their heads!
--I don't hate it.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:10.930
--that these students let things
go to their heads!
--Just come out and say you like it,
would you?

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.100
And as for you...!

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:14.390
You students will immediately--

00:13:14.390 --> 00:13:16.270
Your makeup fell off.

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.070
Immediately return to your rooms!

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:23.440
All right, let's go back
and wake everyone up, Hayama.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:24.400
Yeah.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:26.780
Ah! Just a moment!

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.070
Then, can we join in on your banquet?

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:30.490
Sushi...

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.710
Now, now, it's all right, isn't it?

00:13:36.710 --> 00:13:38.710
Principal...!

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:41.670
Just allowing students to see us
like this will be a problem,

00:13:41.670 --> 00:13:43.710
let alone letting them join us!
If the PTA finds out...

00:13:43.710 --> 00:13:46.380
It'll be fine-fine. It'll be fine-fine.

00:13:46.380 --> 00:13:48.050
I knew you'd say that.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:51.060
Right! Right! It'll be fine-fine!
Ha ha ha, ha!

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.060
Sushi...

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.390
The party starts again,
the party starts again!

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:59.400
That's Principal Narunaru for you!
He understands!

00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:02.020
Narunaru is on the students' side.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:06.110
Principal! Do you think it's good
for this school's educational policy

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:08.410
to allow this to go on!?

00:14:08.410 --> 00:14:12.080
These two are particular
problem children in our school.

00:14:12.080 --> 00:14:13.740
According to what I hear
from the other students,

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.750
they, er, engage in
extremely precocious activities!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.420
What are precocious activities?

00:14:18.420 --> 00:14:20.750
Well, there's [beep] and so on...

00:14:20.750 --> 00:14:23.750
"Beep" doesn't tell me anything.

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:26.420
Keep the jokes limited
to your wrinkles, you hag!

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.720
Still, I think Hayama-kun
has become better-behaved

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.090
since he became friends with Kurata-san.

00:14:30.090 --> 00:14:33.680
So, that's pretty good just by itself.

00:14:33.680 --> 00:14:36.350
Pretty good, you say!?

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:39.350
You two are setting poor examples
for them, aren't you!?

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:40.850
For grade school boys and girls

00:14:40.850 --> 00:14:42.820
to be friendlier with each other
than is necessary is simply--

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:47.030
You should look over, too.

00:14:47.030 --> 00:14:49.360
P- Principal...?

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:51.370
Smushed that mosquito!

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:53.700
Principal! We're discussing
those two right now!

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:55.700
They'll turn out fine-fine.

00:14:55.700 --> 00:14:57.660
There's nothing bad going on, is there?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:15:00.040
I hear that by these
two becoming friends,

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:03.040
the problems in 3rd Class have decreased.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:05.960
As teachers, don't you think it
would be crazy to put a stop to this,

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:10.050
now that things are finally
heading in the right direction?

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:12.720
If you look up close,
he's got a split end.

00:15:12.720 --> 00:15:14.050
The principal...

00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:16.060
...said something principal-like!

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:21.060
Gotcha! Not up to me, not up to me!
They'll turn out fine-fine.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.060
Sana won't be left out! Ha, ha, ha!

00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:24.520
There's no soy sauce.

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.440
"The second day is mountain climbing!!"

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:26.440
Go! Go! Go!

00:15:30.400 --> 00:15:32.360
--Mama, how is the
manuscript coming along?
--Sana-chan, it's not that way!

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:35.450
"Not enough sleep"

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:33.370
Sana is energetically mountain climbing

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:34.240
--Sana is energetically mountain climbing
--Hayama-san, don't go to sleep!

00:15:34.240 --> 00:15:35.450
--on the second day of outdoor school.
--What were you doing last night?

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.700
--on the second day of outdoor school.
--Yodel-ay-hee!!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:37.700
--The scenery here is terribly pretty.
--Yodel-ay-hee!!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.330
"Restrooms"

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:39.200
--The scenery here is terribly pretty.
--Sana-chan, the mountain is this way.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.330
--I wish you could see it too, Mama.
--Sana-chan, the mountain is this way.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:49.380
Um, I can't clean the bathroom
if you work in there.

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:54.390
♪ The faraway stars
that you can see, too... ♪

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:59.060
♪ ...are saying goodbye
to the sun for the day. ♪

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:01.600
--♪ ...are saying goodbye to
the sun for the day. ♪
--Tomorrow is the day we go home.

00:16:01.600 --> 00:16:03.350
--♪ ...are saying goodbye to
the sun for the day. ♪
--I want to go home quickly,
yet at the same time,

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:05.270
--♪ Come tomorrow,
they'll say hello again. ♪
--I don't want to go home at all.

00:16:05.270 --> 00:16:08.070
--♪ Here burns our fire... ♪
--Lately, I've had this strange feeling...

00:16:08.110 --> 00:16:08.530
--♪ Here burns our fire... ♪
--I feel so distant... so agitated...

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:12.070
--♪ The mizu is our water. ♪
--I feel so distant... so agitated...

00:16:12.070 --> 00:16:13.410
♪ Friend-- ♪

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:16.070
Hey, Sana-chan!
You're looking awfully youthful!

00:16:16.070 --> 00:16:20.080
Oh, Zenjiro-chan! How come!? How come!?
"Why"!? What's the deal!?

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:22.080
You-hoo, Sana-chan!

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:24.630
Well, Sana-chan, you were absent
'cause of your outdoo-ah school,

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:27.090
and those of us at Child's Toy
missed you, missed you!

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.250
So we decided to suhprise you

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:32.670
by shooting an "Ambush Sana-chan's
Outdoo-ah School" themed show!

00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:33.680
Look!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.680
Are they shooting a TV show?

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.010
It's Zenjiro!

00:16:36.010 --> 00:16:37.350
Uchiyamada-kun!

00:16:37.350 --> 00:16:40.020
No way! I never heard about this!

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:43.690
Don't be so rigid, Sana-chan.
Your everyday face looks fine.

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:45.690
Aw, you're positively...

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.020
...correct!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.690
--Just kidding!
--Just kidding!

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:52.690
Zenjiro-chan! Uchiyamada-kun!

00:16:52.690 --> 00:16:54.700
Principal!

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.700
Are you sure you should
be allowing this!?

00:16:58.700 --> 00:17:00.040
It will turn out fine-fine.

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:01.700
That's all you ever say.

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:04.710
Does everyone watch Child's Toy!?

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.040
--Yes, we do!
--Of course!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:09.040
Awl right, tonight,
how 'bout we have a bawl togeth-ah!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:10.840
"For some reason,
it's suddenly limbo time!"

00:17:12.380 --> 00:17:14.720
Let's limbo!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:21.640
So, isn't anyone gonna challenge
Uchiyamada-kun here!? Say, with this!

00:17:22.720 --> 00:17:25.060
Can anyone pass und-ah the
height of this milk bottle?

00:17:25.060 --> 00:17:26.400
Now, hold on, you!

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:27.400
What is it, lady?

00:17:27.400 --> 00:17:30.730
What do you take this sacred
educational event for?

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:32.990
The limbo dance is,
by its very nature--!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:37.360
Aah! What kind of outfit
did you put me in!?

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.030
I am adamant! As an educator, I say...

00:17:40.030 --> 00:17:42.200
--Let's limbo!
--Let's limbo!

00:17:43.370 --> 00:17:44.370
This is crazy.

00:17:44.370 --> 00:17:47.920
I don't care how good she is,
it's only as high as a milk bottle.

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.390
There you go!

00:18:04.390 --> 00:18:05.020
Amazing!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.690
Any way you look at it,
her head should have gotten stuck!

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:10.360
It almost seems like they
edited it to fool us!

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:13.400
Okay, now who will meet the challenge
of the height of this matchstick!?

00:18:13.400 --> 00:18:17.610
Don't be ridiculous!
Never mind what I say, let's limbo!

00:18:19.070 --> 00:18:23.040
Ah, a firefly, a firefly.
So pretty, the way it's glowing...

00:18:28.080 --> 00:18:29.370
She disappeared!

00:18:29.370 --> 00:18:31.000
That can't be right!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:34.130
I always thought she
was no ordinary girl,

00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:36.670
and sure enough,
she's an alien or something!

00:18:36.670 --> 00:18:40.340
This week's Sana-chan! Alien-style.
What do you think?

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:41.300
"Caution-- Cliff!"

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:41.600
"Caution-- Cliff!"
A cliff?

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:42.300
A cliff?

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:45.890
Did she fall down it?

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.030
Hey.

00:18:55.030 --> 00:18:58.990
Hayama? Did you fall down, too?
What a fluke.

00:19:00.360 --> 00:19:03.030
I guess we're "two catfish
in the same hole," huh?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:04.700
It's "badgers," you idiot.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.200
"Badger" "Catfish"

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:06.200
Look, they're completely different words.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:09.040
That's one dangerous cliff, huh?

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.370
Ordinarily, you'd die
if you fell down here.

00:19:10.370 --> 00:19:14.290
Hey, we can climb this right away.
This cliff won't giff us any trouble!

00:19:18.050 --> 00:19:19.050
I give up!

00:19:19.050 --> 00:19:21.390
--Hey!!
--Hey!!

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:23.390
--Hey!!
--We fell down here!!

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:24.720
--Hey!!
--Let's limbo!

00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.390
--Hey!!
--You'll do fine-fine!
You'll do fine-fine!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.390
Looks like they can't hear us.

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:31.650
I guess we wait until it quiets down.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.320
This has turned out kind of weird, huh?

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.740
Absolutely. First, I get
lured away by a firefly,

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:43.660
then it turns out I get duped
by the same firefly!

00:19:43.660 --> 00:19:46.330
Come to think of it, it's dangerous
to get too close to him!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:50.460
Oh, no! With just the two of us
in a place like this, I'm...

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.460
...going to be violated!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:20:00.010
Give it up, until it gets quiet up there.

00:20:00.010 --> 00:20:02.010
Whoa! Don't come any closer!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.010
What good will it do to put up a barrier?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:07.970
Whenever you get close, you do
something pervy! I would know, too!

00:20:07.970 --> 00:20:11.020
You've already got
two previous convictions!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:15.360
If you call what I did before pervy,
how are you going to handle your future?

00:20:15.360 --> 00:20:18.020
What kind of remark is that!?
I can't let that one go by!

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:20.360
If you tell me not to do it,
I won't, dummy.

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.320
Okay, don't do anything!

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:25.370
You got it.

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:27.240
You mean it, now?

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:30.950
Come to think of it, I was going
to say something last night.

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.670
Last night, before we went
and joined the teachers.

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:35.670
Oh yeah. What was it?

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:39.340
It occurs to me that you...

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.010
...are good at acting.

00:20:41.010 --> 00:20:43.680
Well, I did train at Komawari, after all!

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.680
So sometimes, I have this thought...

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:49.260
There are times when I think,

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.930
"All of her usual cheerfulness
could be just an act, couldn't it?"

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:57.690
What are you talking about?
That's silly!

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:00.690
I'm not so good at it that I could
act out my whole private life!

00:21:00.690 --> 00:21:02.360
That's something else I think about.

00:21:02.360 --> 00:21:04.360
Then why would you say such a thing?

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:08.450
I'm just saying... I have that
passing thought once in a while.

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.580
Maybe it does come
into play a little bit.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:18.590
But then, doesn't everybody do that?
Still...

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:25.050
when I'm not especially cheerful,
I get told that I'm being un-Sana-like!

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:28.050
So I have to stay cheerful all the time!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.810
Something has happened, hasn't it?

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:35.140
You're worried about something, huh?

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:40.070
Is that how I look?

00:21:40.070 --> 00:21:41.360
Mm-hmm.

00:21:44.740 --> 00:21:47.740
How come Hayama is the
only one who noticed?

00:21:47.740 --> 00:21:49.320
What happened?

00:21:52.740 --> 00:21:55.080
--I don't even know
where to begin explaining.
--(I- I feel sort of strange.)

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:57.830
--Is it that complicated?
--(I guess I'm a little nervous.)

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:00.040
Maybe it's because nobody
has ever asked me

00:22:00.040 --> 00:22:03.420
if I was worrying
about something before.

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:05.420
I'm feeling a little on edge.

00:22:05.420 --> 00:22:08.180
Mm-hmm, about what?

00:22:11.760 --> 00:22:12.600
You know what...?

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:15.730
How about we fulfill
your promise, Sana?

00:22:16.980 --> 00:22:21.980
Mama is writing an essay on me...
all about me...

00:22:21.980 --> 00:22:22.980
Essay?

00:22:22.980 --> 00:22:25.320
Once this essay comes out...

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:28.990
...the enjoyable life
that Mama and I share...

00:22:28.990 --> 00:22:32.450
...could be completely destroyed!

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:42.250
"Back against the wall."

00:22:42.750 --> 00:22:47.760
That's what you say about times like these.

00:22:49.010 --> 00:22:52.510
In dire straits,

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:56.100
I've been waiting for an answer.

00:22:56.600 --> 00:22:59.980
My confessions are worked out
long in advance,

00:23:00.940 --> 00:23:05.070
to always go along with the scenario.

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:11.110
My heart may be settled, but my mind is in a...

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:13.280
...panic!!

00:23:14.280 --> 00:23:19.120
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:19.330 --> 00:23:21.830
he's there.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.090
And our usual classroom...

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:27.710
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.220
...for two.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:33.680
Although I've said nothing but wisecracks...

00:23:33.890 --> 00:23:38.430
...up to now, just for today,

00:23:39.350 --> 00:23:42.020
I'm going to be honest and sincere,

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:46.730
so BOY, take a look my way!

00:23:47.650 --> 00:23:52.320
When my friends invite me by, suddenly,

00:23:52.490 --> 00:23:54.990
he's there,

00:23:55.910 --> 00:23:58.160
And our usual classroom...

00:23:58.370 --> 00:24:00.710
...quick-changes into a merry-go-round...

00:24:00.870 --> 00:24:03.250
...for two.

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:10.260
Hoy! In Sana-chan's next adventures...

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:11.880
After following after a firefly,
I fell down a cliff.

00:24:11.880 --> 00:24:13.300
I felt relieved after
what Hayama had to say,

00:24:13.300 --> 00:24:15.470
and then while we ran around,
I lost sight of the fireflies,

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:17.850
then climbed back up the cliff,
but the limbo dance was over!

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.390
Summer vacation! Summer vacation!

00:24:19.390 --> 00:24:20.850
Shooting a commercial,
I meet Kamura Naozumi!

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:23.520
Kamura Naozumi? Who are you!?

00:24:23.520 --> 00:24:27.520
Next time on Kodomo no Omocha, Episode 15;
the fated series marches on!

00:24:27.520 --> 00:24:31.530
The Summer of My Promise- Part II

00:24:31.530 --> 00:24:34.160
There'll be even more...
yadda yadda, etc. etc...
